  "comparison_analysis": "MULTI-MODEL COMPARISON ANALYSIS\n==================================================\n\nDataset: 20000 NAV-derived samples, 16 engineered features, 6 classes\nSplit: 60% train / 20% validation / 20% test (stratified)\nSeed: 42\n\nMETRIC SUMMARY:\nModel                  Accuracy    Bal.Acc   Macro-F1        MCC\n--------------------------------------------------------------\nRandomForest             0.9563     0.9221     0.9144     0.9393\nPyTorch_MLP              0.9560     0.9126     0.9174     0.9390\nFT_Transformer           0.9705     0.9220     0.9331     0.9590\n\nBest Accuracy:          FT_Transformer (0.9705)\nBest Balanced Accuracy: RandomForest (0.9221)\nBest Macro F1:          FT_Transformer (0.9331)\nBest MCC:               FT_Transformer (0.9590)\n\nCONCLUSION: FT_Transformer achieved the best aggregate performance.\n\nThe neural network's advantage may stem from its ability to model non-linear\nfeature interactions that the tree ensemble's axis-aligned splits miss.\n\nNOTE: The MLP and FT-Transformer were trained for a reduced number of epochs\n(50 and 30 respectively) on CPU due to compute constraints.\nThese are NOT converged models. With GPU training and full hyperparameter search,\nthe neural networks may close the gap or surpass the RF, but the committed\nnumbers reflect only what was actually measured."
